===Speak with the people in the plaza and gather clues{{subst:void|<!--201190305-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=adventure|location=Administrative District|update|The microfilm used to display projections was stolen. Without this film, the History Exhibit cannot open to the public.<br />Bronya had stated that she will wholeheartedly support further investigations of these cases.<br />Head to the Administrative District Plaza to assess the passers-by, and see whether some of them have relevant clues.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
----
:'''Pela:''' *sigh* Another half day gone, and nothing to show for it...
:'''Pela:''' Ugh, the culprit is still hiding in the shadows. Can't we find even one lead?
:'''???:''' Ah! If it isn't Belobog's most adorable public servant &mdash; and the magnificent outsider! Good day to you!
:'''Pela:''' ...You know us?
----
:'''Wallace:''' Young lady, I have seen you on many occasions near the Everwinter Monument, teaching children the history of Belobog. I am truly in awe of your knowledge and patience!
:'''Pela:''' Hehe, okay... thanks for the compliment, I guess. May I ask, with whom do we have the pleasure of speaking?
:'''Wallace:''' I am Wallace Cambridge Limestein, the 25th head of the Limestein family. I am honored to make your acquaintance!
:'''Wallace:''' And yes, I am familiar with this outsider next to you &mdash; {{MC|ж=she|м=he}} often walks right past me without so much as a greeting.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Are you holding a grudge!?
::'''Wallace:''' How could you say such a thing!? I just want everyone to have a proper understanding of basic manners.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I Don't Even Know Who You Are!
::'''Wallace:''' I am Wallace Cambridge Limestein, the 25th head of the Lime&mdash;
:'''Pela:''' Alright, alright, we got it. Mr. Limestein, is there something you want to discuss with us?
:'''Wallace:''' Oh, as a matter of fact, I do. I noticed you two had been wandering around Administrative District Plaza for some time now, stopping to ask questions at every turn, so I surmised you were investigating something important.
:'''Wallace:''' As it so happens, I witnessed a strange incident recently that left me quite puzzled... After reflecting on it for a time, I decided it would be most appropriate to inform public officials.
:'''Pela:''' This incident... is it related to the museum thefts?
:'''Wallace:''' I can't say for sure that it's directly related, but a friend of mine I no longer hear from used to frequent the museum, and often talked about its exhibits with a group of us tea lovers.
:'''Pela:''' So by "no longer hear from," you mean you've been unable to get in touch with this friend of yours?
:'''Wallace:''' Precisely! His name is Norbert &mdash; we used to chat during lunch breaks in the lobby of the Goethe Hotel &mdash; along with a few other high-class individuals, of course.
:'''Wallace:''' And one day, Norbert suddenly stopped showing up to our tea parties. It was as though he disappeared into thin air. I still remember the last thing he said to me...
:'''Wallace:''' "Limestein, listen to me &mdash; one must be ambitious in life. I'm gonna do something big for once!"
:'''Pela:''' "Be ambitious in life, do something big for once..." Coming from the mouth of a wealthy gentleman, that sounded rather curious to me.
:'''Pela:''' This Norbert guy, do you know what his line of work was?
:'''Wallace:''' I'm not entirely sure &mdash; I never asked.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Weren't the two of you friends?
::'''Wallace:''' You wouldn't understand &mdash; friendship between gentlemen is as pure as water. We are all dignified people, why bother with such trivial matters?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So more like a drinking buddy than a friend...
::'''Wallace:''' What a preposterous statement! You wouldn't understand &mdash; friendship between gentlemen is as pure as water. We are all dignified people, why bother with such trivial matters?
:'''Pela:''' Ugh... In the eyes of most people, there's a world of difference between "trivial matters" and a career.
:'''Pela:''' ...I have recorded all the clues you provided, Mr. Limestein. Thank you for putting your trust in the Silvermane Guards. We will keep you informed if there are any developments in the investigation.
:'''Wallace:''' No, no, I should be thanking you, young lady of the Guards. Well then, if that's all, I shall take my leave.
----
:'''Pela:''' I wonder if this "friend" of Mr. Wallace has anything to do with the museum thefts...
:'''Pela:''' That's enough detective work for today &mdash; questioning more people will just be a waste of energy. (Trailblazer), let's go report back to Lady Bronya.
----
{{Dialogue End}}

===Head to Qlipoth Fort and report to Bronya{{subst:void|<!--201190310-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=adventure|location=Qlipoth Fort|update|The microfilm used to display projections was stolen. Without this film, the History Exhibit cannot open to the public.<br />You heard from the rich boy Wallace that his "friend" Norbert has been acting strange lately. Perhaps this is related to the exhibit thefts?<br />No matter what, you should bring this news to Bronya.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
----
:'''Pela:''' Miss Bronya, we're back.
:'''Bronya:''' Thank you both for your hard work. Did you find out anything in the Administrative District?
:'''Pela:''' We didn't find anything directly related to the museum thefts, but there was one thing worth noting...
:{{Black Screen|Tell Bronya about Wallace's disappearing "friend."}}
:'''Bronya:''' I see. It was the man from the Limestein family who provided the information.
:'''Bronya:''' Norbert... Norbert... I feel like I've heard that name somewhere before. Please, give me a moment to see if I can recall...
:'''Bronya:''' ...Ah, I remember now. The Minister of Transportation, Noel, has a nephew named Norbert &mdash; I believe he's currently working in the Municipal Department as a transportation coordinator.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You can remember all of that!?
::'''Bronya:''' The leader of a city should be familiar with the status and division of labor of her subordinates &mdash; that's just part of the job. Norbert's position is indeed an idle one, so it's no wonder he has time to socialize with members of the Limestein family.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Guess he comes from old money too?
::'''Bronya:''' Norbert's position is indeed an idle one &mdash; it's no wonder he has time to socialize with members of the Limestein family.
:'''Bronya:''' If what Wallace said is right, then Norbert must have been missing for several days already. There must be someone who knows where he is.
:'''Bronya:''' Even if they want to keep the young man's secret... they'll cough it up with the right kind of encouragement.
:'''Bronya:''' Kyle, can I ask you a favor? I would like you to visit the residence of Minister Noel and ask around regarding the whereabouts of Mr. Norbert.
:'''Soldier Kyle:''' Understood, Madam Guardian!
:{{Black Screen|After some time, Kyle heads back to Qlipoth Fort...}}
:'''Soldier Kyle:''' Lady Bronya, Miss Pela, I have returned.
:'''Bronya:''' You were quite expedient, Kyle. Did you find anything out from the Department of Transportation?
:'''Soldier Kyle:''' It took a little prodding, but a few of the more timid attendants started speaking up...
:'''Soldier Kyle:''' They say that Mr. Norbert was indeed leaving at odd hours recently. Whenever someone would ask where he was headed, he'd mumble something about going to the shopping street to "inspect the site."
:'''Soldier Kyle:''' The attendants think he might have a love interest &mdash; someone he doesn't want his family to know about &mdash; they haven't mentioned anything to the Minister of Transportation.
:'''Bronya:''' Going out at unusual hours, the shopping street, could it be...
----
:'''Bronya:''' ...Pela, (Trailblazer) &mdash; I have a request. I'd like the two of you to scout out {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|Backwater Pass}} and see whether anything's happening there.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why there?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Does Norbert have anything to do with our investigation?
:'''Bronya:''' While the two of you were busy questioning people in the city, I received some tip-offs. One source said that suspicious people were recently seen sneaking around the Fragmentum corrosion zone, and that the Silvermane Guards didn't prevent them from entering.
:'''Bronya:''' Together with Norbert's mumblings about a "shopping street..." I think all these clues are pointing in one direction.
:'''Pela:''' ...So this Mr. Norbert could well be the museum thief we're looking for?
:'''Pela:''' ...We can't hold off a moment longer! Hurry, (Trailblazer), let's go arrest that scoundrel.
:'''Bronya:''' My apologies, I have a lot of business to attend to at present &mdash; I won't be joining you. Good luck recovering the stolen items.
----

;(Talk to Pela)
----
:'''Pela:''' (Trailblazer), we can't delay a moment longer. We need to move now.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Let's head out.
:{{Диалог|Выход}} I need a little while.
::'''Pela:''' ...Okay, whenever you're ready, but don't take too long!
;(Unused &mdash; Raid201190311_ClosePage)

{{Dialogue End}}

===Interact with Pela and prepare to go to Backwater Pass{{subst:void|<!--201190311-->}}===
